---
layout: page
title: {{ page }} Avalanche Danger Report Interactive Map
description: Autogenerated DEM Shading rules for each advisory zone in {{ page }} for quickly adding avalanche danger and problem layers in CalTopo.
tool: avy
image:
  path: /assets/images/avy-layers.png
  width: 175
  height: 131
js_includes:
  - https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js
  - avy.js
css_includes:
 - https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css
---

<!-- Looking out for you... -->

<section class="measure center lh-copy f5-ns f6 ph2 mv3" style="text-align: justify;">
    <strong>"Where's the danger?"</strong> Here are autogenerated DEM Shading rules for each advisory zone that allow for quickly adding avalanche danger and problem layers to CalTopo maps.
</section>

<p id="settings-toggle" class="mw5 b center tc hover-light-red black-70 pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="settings">Show Instructions</p>
<section id="settings" class="overflow-hidden" style="display:none;">
    <div class="mv2 ph2 center">
        <div class="fn f6 tc">
            <p class="measure lh-copy center"><a class="no-underline fancy-link relative light-red" href="https://training.caltopo.com/all_users/base-layers/custom2#dem">Digital Elevation Model (DEM)</a> shading lets you create custom shading schemes based on elevation, slope, aspect and tree cover.</p>
            <p class="measure lh-copy center">These layers are built on relatively low resolution elevation data, so small terrain features and exact slope angles won't always show up. For higher definition terrain analysis (lidar-based), check out <a class="no-underline fancy-link relative light-red" href="https://www.aspectavy.com/">AspectAvy</a> (not affiliated).</p>
            <hr class="mw5 p0 mv2 o-60 b0 bt b--light-red light-red bg-light-red">
            <p class="measure lh-copy center"><strong>Avalanche Report</strong></p>
            <p class="measure lh-copy center">
                The selected elevation bands are not meant to be exact, but represent a characteristic of the terrain which varies locally.
            </p>
            <p class="measure lh-copy center">
                The highest band, <b>ATL</b> (<i>Above Tree Line</i>), typically includes alpine areas beginning as the treeline transitions into open slopes extending to ridges and peaks.
            </p>
            <p class="measure lh-copy center">
                The middle band, <b>NTL</b> (<i>Near Tree Line</i>), is typically a narrow transition zone between dense forests and treeless alpine areas.
            </p>
            <p class="measure lh-copy center">
                The lowest band, <b>BTL</b> (<i>Below Tree Line</i>), typically extends from valley floors or snowline to near treeline.
            </p>
            <hr class="mw5 p0 mv2 o-60 b0 bt b--light-red light-red bg-light-red">
            <p class="measure lh-copy center"><b>Usage</b></p>
            <p class="measure lh-copy center">
                You'll find that <b>Terrain Modeling</b> in the left pane will show layers that can be turned on and edited. The right pane will show <b>Custom Layers</b> that can be toggled on or off.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div>
    <div class="mt4 ph2 tc">
        <label for="zoneSel" class="f6 b">Select A Zone:</label>
        <select class="f6 ma1 bg-near-white pa2" id="zoneSel">
            {% for zone in zones %}
            <option value="{{ zone.slug }}" title="{{ zone.name }}" {% if loop.first %}selected=""{% endif %}>{{ zone.short_name | default(zone.name) }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="flex flex-column flex-row-ns">
    <div id="regional_zones" class="ph3 w-100 w-50-ns">
        {% for zone in zones %}
        <div id="{{ zone.slug }}-report" class="avy-zone{% if not loop.first %} dn{% endif %}" data-id="{{ zone.slug }}" data-color="{{ zone.color }}"{% if zone.has_subregions %} data-subregions="true"{% endif %} data-published="{{ zone.published }}">
            <h3 class="tc bb b--moon-gray">Avalanche Report</h3>
            {% if zone.short_name and zone.short_name != zone.name %}
            <details class="tc f6 black-70 mt0 mb3">
                <summary class="pointer" title="Show all areas">{{ zone.short_name }}</summary>
                <p class="mt2 mb0 lh-copy">{{ zone.name }}</p>
            </details>
            {% endif %}
            {% if zone.danger %}
            <div id="{{ zone.slug }}-title" class="mv4 tc">
                <div><a id="{{ zone.slug }}-url" class="no-underline black-70 pa2 hover-light-red b--moon-gray bg-light-gray ba" target="_blank" href="https://caltopo.com/map.html#ll={{ zone.geo[1] }},{{ zone.geo[0] }}&z=10&b=mbt&{{ zone.layers }}">Pre-populated CalTopo Map</a></div>
            </div>
            {% if zone.grm %}
            <dl class="f6">
                <dt>
                    <strong>{{ sun_day }} Steep Terrain To Avoid (GRM)</strong>
                    <div class="tooltip dib v-top pl2"><a data-clipboard-text="{{ zone.grm[0] | join('&#10;') }}" onclick="clickFunc(this, 'grm-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}'); return false;" onmouseout="outFunc('grm-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}')" onblur="outFunc('grm-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}')" href="#" role="button" aria-label="Copy GRM rules"><span class="tooltiptext" id="grm-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}" aria-live="polite">Copy rules</span><img style="width: 15px;" src="/assets/images/svg/copy-icon.svg" alt=""></a></div>
                </dt>
                <dd class="ml3">
                    <ul class="list pl0 mt1 mb0 code f7">
                    {% for row in zone.grm[2] %}
                        <li class="pv1"><div style="clear: both;background-color: {{ row.color }}" class="fl mr2 h1 w1"></div> {{ row.level }}: caution {{ row.caution }}&deg;+, avoid {{ row.avoid }}&deg;+</li>
                    {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                    <p class="f7 black-60 lh-copy mt2 mb0">Slope angle limits from the <a class="no-underline fancy-link relative light-red" href="https://whiterisk.ch/info/en/help/tour-planning/cruxes">Graphical Reduction Method</a>, applied to the regional forecast. Band edges are blurred &plusmn;500' and aspects &plusmn;22.5&deg;, taking the worse rating. This is not slope-scale danger: it doesn't account for spatial variability, connected terrain or runouts. Check the terrain above and below you.</p>
                </dd>
            </dl>
            {% endif %}
            <dl class="f6">
                <dt>
                    <strong>{{ sun_day }} Avalanche Danger</strong>
                    {#- UT stores each band's layer as a list of rules, other centers as one string #}
                    {%- set ns = namespace(lines=[]) %}
                    {%- for rule in zone.danger | reverse %}
                    {%- set ns.lines = ns.lines + ([rule.layer] if rule.layer is string else rule.layer | list) %}
                    {%- endfor %}
                    <div class="tooltip dib v-top pl2"><a data-clipboard-text="{{ ns.lines | join('&#10;') }}" onclick="clickFunc(this, 'danger-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}'); return false;" onmouseout="outFunc('danger-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}')" onblur="outFunc('danger-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}')" href="#" role="button" aria-label="Copy danger rules"><span class="tooltiptext" id="danger-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}" aria-live="polite">Copy rules</span><img style="width: 15px;" src="/assets/images/svg/copy-icon.svg" alt=""></a></div>
                </dt>
                <dd class="ml3">
                    <ul class="list pl0 mt1 mb0 code f7 rules-{{ zone.slug }}">
                    {% for rule in zone.danger|reverse %}
                        <li class="pv1 {{ rule.id }}">
                            <div style="clear: both;" class="dynamic-color fl mr2 h1 w1"
                            {% for color in rule.colors %}
                                data-color{{ loop.index }}="{{ color }}"
                            {% endfor %}
                            ></div> <span class="desc">{{ rule.desc }}</span>
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                    <p class="f7 black-60 lh-copy mt2 mb0">Danger ratings are regional. Each rating covers a whole elevation band across the forecast zone, not any single slope, and danger varies within a band. Band edges are drawn here at fixed elevations, but treeline shifts with aspect, terrain and local weather. A Low or Moderate rating doesn't mean every slope is safe: isolated dangerous slopes can exist at any level. Use the rating to set expectations for the day, not to pick slopes.</p>
                </dd>
            </dl>
            {% else %}
            {% if zone.report_access is sameas false %}
            <div class="avy-note-wrap">
                <div class="shadow-5 dark-blue bg-lightest-blue bl bw3 b--dark-blue mv3 tl lh-copy" style="border-radius: 5px; font-size: 1.05em; padding: .1em 1.75em;" role="note">
                    <p class="i" style="margin: .8em 0;"><b>Note:</b> Danger and problem layers aren't available here, as this site doesn't have access to the {{ zone.center_name }}'s forecast data. Please visit the <a class="no-underline fancy-link relative dark-blue b" href="{{ zone.url }}">{{ zone.center_name }}</a> for the latest forecast.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            {% else %}
            <div class="pv4 ph2 tc ba b--moon-gray">{{ zone.message }}</div>
            {% endif %}
            {% endif %}

            {% if zone.problems %}
            <dl class="f6">
                {% for problem in zone.problems %}
                    <dt class="mt3">
                        <strong>{{ problem.name }}</strong>
                        <div class="tooltip dib v-top pl2"><a data-clipboard-text="{{ problem.rules | map(attribute='layer') | reverse | join('&#10;') }}" onclick="clickFunc(this, 'problem-{{ loop.index }}-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}'); return false;" onmouseout="outFunc('problem-{{ loop.index }}-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}')" onblur="outFunc('problem-{{ loop.index }}-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}')" href="#" role="button" aria-label="Copy {{ problem.name }} rules"><span class="tooltiptext" id="problem-{{ loop.index }}-tooltip-{{ zone.slug }}" aria-live="polite">Copy rules</span><img style="width: 15px;" src="/assets/images/svg/copy-icon.svg" alt=""></a></div>
                    </dt>
                    <dd class="ml3">
                        <ul class="list pl0 mt1 mb0 code f7 rules-{{ zone.slug }}">
                        {% for rule in problem.rules|reverse %}
                            <li class="pv1 {{ rule.id }}">
                                <div style="clear: both;background-color: {{ rule.color }}" class="fl mr2 h1 w1"></div> <span class="desc">{{ rule.desc }}</span>
                            </li>
                        {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </dd>
                {% endfor %}
            </dl>
            <p class="f7 black-60 lh-copy mt2">Problem aspects and elevations show where the forecaster expects each problem to be most widespread or most sensitive, not hard boundaries. A problem can also exist on neighboring aspects and elevations, and unshaded slopes aren't free of it. The shading cuts off at exact compass degrees, but gullies, ridges and convex rolls face many directions within one slope. A slope outside the shading can still be threatened by a shaded slope above it. Read the forecast's problem description for likelihood, size and distribution.</p>
            {% endif %}

            {% if (zone.danger or zone.problems) and zone.confidence in ("medium", "low") %}
            <div class="f6 black-70 bl bw2 {{ 'b--gold bg-washed-yellow' if zone.confidence == 'medium' else 'b--light-red bg-washed-red' }} pa2 br2 mv3 lh-copy" role="note">
                <b>{{ zone.confidence | title }} confidence elevation bands.</b>
                {% if zone.confidence == "medium" -%}
                {{ zone.center_name }} doesn't publish numeric elevation bands, so these are derived from elevations mentioned in its past forecasts.
                {%- else -%}
                No published elevation bands were found for this zone, so these are a rough estimate.
                {%- endif %}
                Adjust them in CalTopo by editing the layer.
            </div>
            {% endif %}
            {% if (zone.danger and zone.published) or zone.report_access is not sameas false %}
            <div class="bg-near-white br2 ph3 pv2 mt4 tc black-60">
            {% if zone.danger and zone.published %}
            <p class="f7 mv1">
                <strong>Issued at:</strong> {{ zone.published }}
            </p>
            {% endif %}
            {% if zone.report_access is not sameas false %}
            <p class="f7 mv1 measure center">
                Forecast data from <a class="no-underline fancy-link relative dark-gray b" href="{{ zone.center_link }}">{{ zone.center_name }}</a>. This site is not affiliated with or endorsed by them. Read the <a class="no-underline fancy-link relative dark-gray b" href="{{ zone.url }}">full forecast</a> before heading out.
            </p>
            {% endif %}
            </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="ph3 w-100 w-50-ns">
        <h3 class="tc bb b--moon-gray">Zone</h3>
        <div style="height: 300px;" id="map"></div>
        {% for zone in zones %}
        <div id="{{ zone.slug }}-shape" data-geojson="/assets/json/avalanche-zones/{{ zone.slug }}.geojson" class="avy-zone{% if not loop.first %} dn{% endif %}">
            <div class="mt1 tc"><a class="no-underline fancy-link relative light-red f6" target="_blank" href="/assets/json/avalanche-zones/{{ zone.slug }}.geojson" download="">Download GeoJSON</a></div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</div>

<hr id="hr-0" class="mw5 p0 mv4 o-70 b0 bt b--light-red light-red bg-light-red">
<section class="tc lh-copy">
    <label for="regionSel" class="f6 b">Change Regions:</label>
    <select class="f6 ma1 bg-near-white pa2" id="regionSel">
        {% for state in states %}
        {% if state.active %}
        <option value="{{ state.page }}.html"{% if state.name == page %} selected=""{% endif %}>{{ state.name }}</option>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        <option value="/avy/canada.html">Canada</option>
    </select>
</section>

{% raw %}
{% include feedback.html %}
{% endraw %}

<p id="issues-toggle" class="mw5 b center tc hover-light-red black-70 pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="issues">Show Known Issues</p>
<section id="issues" class="overflow-hidden tc f6" aria-live="polite">
</section>
